</td><td>&#x02212;&#x02009;0.131</td></tr><tr><td><italic>P</italic> value</td><td>0.11</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></p></sec><sec id="Sec18"><title>Predictors for high remodeling index</title><p id="Par36">Multivariate linear regression analysis was done for prediction of remodeling index. Variance inflation factor (VIF) was used to assess collinearity. VIF of all factors were below 5, indicating no multicollinearity problems in the model.</p><p id="Par37">By linear regression analysis; positive family history, diabetes mellitus, low HDL, HBA1c, and plaque burden% were predictors of high remodeling index (Table&#x000a0;<xref rid="Tab2" ref-type="table">2</xref>).<table-wrap id="Tab2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Linear regression analysis for remodeling index (RI)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th/><th>
